[about]
Title=09 - Glossary
Intro=The words EdSharp uses, in alphabetical order. I say the term; the reader says what it means. Each is one line, for looking up or for listening straight through.
Setup=Nothing is needed.
Homework=Pick three terms you did not know and find each one in EdSharp.

[step]

Say=address.
Key=
Hear=Where the cursor is: line, column and percent of the document. Alt plus A.

[step]

Say=Alternate Menu.
Key=
Hear=Every command in one list you type into, with its key beside it. Alt plus F10.

[step]

Say=block.
Key=
Hear=A stretch of code at one indentation. Control plus B goes to the next; Alt plus B reads the rest of this one.

[step]

Say=bookmark.
Key=
Hear=A place in a file, kept with the file. Control plus K sets one; Alt plus K returns to it.

[step]

Say=chunk.
Key=
Hear=A run of characters with no space in it. Alt plus Right Arrow goes to the next; Control plus Space selects it.

[step]

Say=compiler.
Key=
Hear=The program EdSharp hands your file to with Control plus F5, chosen once by extension with Control plus Shift plus F5.

[step]

Say=configuration options.
Key=
Hear=The one dialog of settings -- spell checker, font, speech, the AI model. Alt plus Shift plus C.

[step]

Say=convert file format.
Key=
Hear=Converting a file on disk without opening it, one or many at a time. Control plus Shift plus V.

[step]

Say=current windows.
Key=
Hear=The list of open documents, to pick one. F4; Shift plus F4 says their titles.

[step]

Say=document.
Key=
Hear=One file open in EdSharp, in a window of its own; Control plus Tab moves to the next, F4 lists them.

[step]

Say=Elevate Version.
Key=
Hear=Checking for a newer EdSharp and installing it. F11, because elevate sounds like eleven.

[step]

Say=encoding.
Key=
Hear=How a file's characters are stored. Alt plus Z twice says it; Alt plus Shift plus Y renders the text in another one.

[step]

Say=export.
Key=
Hear=Writing the document out as another format -- a web page, a Word document, plain text. Alt plus Shift plus E.

[step]

Say=file find.
Key=
Hear=Searching a folder of files for a string and opening the one you pick. Alt plus Shift plus F.

[step]

Say=hotkey summary.
Key=
Hear=Every command with its key and description, in a new window. Alt plus Shift plus H.

[step]

Say=Key Describer.
Key=
Hear=A mode in which every key says what it does instead of doing it. Control plus F1 turns it on and off.

[step]

Say=Ollama.
Key=
Hear=The program that runs AI models on your own computer; EdSharp's F12, Shift plus F12 and Alt plus Shift plus F7 talk to it.

[step]

Say=open other format.
Key=
Hear=Opening a Word document, PDF, slide deck or spreadsheet converted to text. Control plus Shift plus O.

[step]

Say=preview.
Key=
Hear=Markdown shown as a formatted page in a window of EdSharp's own. Control plus F9.

[step]

Say=regular expression.
Key=
Hear=A pattern that matches many strings -- every number, every line starting with a dash. Control plus F3 finds with one; Control plus Shift plus R replaces.

[step]

Say=result window.
Key=
Hear=A document EdSharp opens with the output of a compile, an AI answer or a summary; read-only until you say otherwise.

[step]

Say=run.
Key=
Hear=Executing the current file by its extension. F5; Shift plus F5 runs the address at the cursor.

[step]

Say=say status.
Key=
Hear=Whether the document has changed since it was saved; pressed twice, its encoding. Alt plus Z.

[step]

Say=session log.
Key=
Hear=What EdSharp did this session, kept under your local application data. Control plus F12 copies its path for a report.

[step]

Say=snippet.
Key=
Hear=A saved piece of text or code, pasted or run with Alt plus V, saved with Alt plus S.

[step]

Say=yield.
Key=
Hear=The size of the text: characters, words and lines, for all of it or the selection. Alt plus Y.

[step]

Say=Twenty-six terms. The guide, F1, has each of them in context.
Key=
Hear=
